cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this code, please cite it using the metadata below. Once the
  accompanying paper is published, please cite the paper instead; a
  preferred-citation block will be added here at that point.
title: >-
  Analysis code for apolipoprotein B goal assignment and attainment under
  the 2026 ACC/AHA dyslipidemia guideline (NHANES 2005-2016)
abstract: >-
  R code implementing Figure 1 of the 2026 ACC/AHA dyslipidemia guideline
  across six NHANES cycles (2005-2016), and computing apolipoprotein B goal
  assignment, goal attainment, and the associated sensitivity analyses.
  Because Figure 1's patient-population rows overlap and the guideline states
  no precedence rule, goals are assigned by an order-independent union rule:
  a goal applies if any matched row states one, and where matched rows differ
  the most stringent value applies. No data are distributed; the NHANES cycles
  and the NCHS linked mortality files are downloaded from CDC at run time.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vishal
    family-names: Parackal
    affiliation: >-
      Division of Cardiology, Lahey Hospital and Medical Center,
      Beth Israel Lahey Health, Burlington, Massachusetts, USA
  - given-names: Arjun
    family-names: Jayakumar
    affiliation: >-
      Division of Cardiology, Lahey Hospital and Medical Center,
      Beth Israel Lahey Health, Burlington, Massachusetts, USA
license: MIT
keywords:
  - apolipoprotein B
  - dyslipidemia
  - clinical practice guidelines
  - guideline implementation
  - NHANES
  - complex survey analysis
  - cardiovascular disease prevention
  - reproducible research

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TO COMPLETE BEFORE, OR JUST AFTER, THE FIRST PUSH
#
#   repository-code: the GitHub URL, once the repository exists, e.g.
#     repository-code: "https://github.com/<user>/<repo>"
#
#   version and date-released: fill these when you tag a release. Cutting a
#     release is also what triggers Zenodo to mint the DOI the manuscript's
#     Data Sharing Statement promises, e.g.
#     version: "1.0.0"
#     date-released: "2026-09-15"
#
#   doi: the Zenodo DOI, once minted.
#
#   orcid: add under each author if you have one, as
#     orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"
#     Deliberately omitted rather than guessed.
#
# ON PUBLICATION, add a preferred-citation block so that citing the code
# resolves to the paper:
#
#   preferred-citation:
#     type: article
#     title: "<the paper's title>"
#     authors: [<the full author list, in byline order>]
#     journal: "JAMA Cardiology"
#     year: 2026
#     doi: "<the article DOI>"
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
